From 1ccfadabbd778727a62abdea1693df19b99c7c45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jo Dagnault <jdagnault@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:20:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] elanpress: Handle blocking finger queries and sharpen
 matching

Tested on an ASUS Vivobook M7400QC (04f3:0c6e, bcdDevice 5.00, sensor
FW 0x0500), where the driver as first written could not enroll and,
once it could, accepted a different finger of the same person.

Capture:

* This firmware never answers the finger-status query (0x40 0x3f) while
  no finger is on the sensor; the read simply blocks until a touch
  arrives, and then answers 0x55 on every query. The driver waited for
  a non-0x55 "finger off" byte that never came and spun forever. Treat
  a timed-out status read as "no finger" so both firmware flavours work,
  and re-issue the query every 500 ms while waiting for a touch instead
  of one open-ended read.
* Send the stop command (with a short settle, see MR !647) before each
  capture, as the elan driver does between captures.
* Log the firmware version at open and the sensor's calibration mean and
  status after the background frame, and dump raw frames to
  $ELANPRESS_DUMP_DIR when set, for offline analysis.

Matching:

* The sensor's response compresses towards a ceiling around 8900 counts
  as the finger settles, so a heavy or moist press loses ridge contrast
  within 100-300 ms. Use the frame with the most ridge-band energy
  instead of averaging the middle of the touch. (Calibrating the sensor
  with the finger on only shifts a global offset; it does not recover
  the contrast.)
* The contact-pressure envelope dominated the correlation, so any two
  fingers correlated at 0.7-0.9. High-pass the image (sigma 1.5) and
  normalise local contrast before correlating; store the result as int8.
  Print format version 2, old prints are rejected.
* With the new representation, on 21 genuine and 26 impostor presses
  across four sessions (including the mirror-similar other index
  finger), impostors stay <= 0.52 and genuine presses on an enrolled
  region score 0.67-0.86; threshold 0.60.

Enrollment:

* The sensor sees about 7.5x2.6 mm, so verification only works where a
  stored touch overlaps the probe. Enroll 16 touches instead of 8 and
  reject a touch whose similarity to a stored one exceeds 0.75 with a
  retry, so the user is made to move the finger between touches.
* Reject touches with almost no ridge structure (high-pass RMS < 30).

